WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.209 --> 00:00:19.532
Marius had entered Monsieur Gillenormand's house with little hope.

2
00:00:20.192 --> 00:00:22.314
He exited it in deep despair.

3
00:00:22.954 --> 00:00:26.817
He began to walk the streets of Paris, not knowing what else to do.

4
00:00:27.757 --> 00:00:31.200
At two o'clock in the morning, he returned to Courfeyrac's apartment.

5
00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:36.782
Marius threw himself on his mattress fully dressed; it was dawn before he fell asleep.

6
00:00:37.723 --> 00:00:40.264
When Marius woke up, Courfeyrac was there.

7
00:00:40.944 --> 00:00:44.025
So were two other friends, Enjolras and Combeferre.

8
00:00:44.626 --> 00:00:46.446
The three of them were getting ready to go out.

9
00:00:46.466 --> 00:00:48.307
"Are you coming with us?"

10
00:00:48.807 --> 00:00:49.648
asked Courfeyrac.

11
00:00:50.488 --> 00:00:51.548
Marius shook his head.

12
00:00:52.269 --> 00:00:55.990
Sometime after they left, he put Javert's pistol into his pocket.

13
00:00:56.691 --> 00:01:01.785
After a while he went out and roamed the streets again, dark thoughts flooding his mind.

14
00:01:02.906 --> 00:01:05.487
At nine o'clock he arrived at the house on the Rue Plumet.

15
00:01:06.147 --> 00:01:09.069
It had been 48 hours since he had last seen Cosette.

16
00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:14.552
Now he was going to see her again, and all other thoughts faded away.

17
00:01:16.113 --> 00:01:18.915
He pushed aside the bar on the gate and entered the garden.

18
00:01:19.495 --> 00:01:22.597
Cosette was not in the spot where she usually waited for him.

19
00:01:22.617 --> 00:01:26.639
"She must be waiting for me on the bench," he said to himself.

20
00:01:27.539 --> 00:01:28.500
But she was not there.

21
00:01:29.024 --> 00:01:30.145
He looked up at the house.

22
00:01:30.826 --> 00:01:32.167
All the shutters were closed.

23
00:01:32.627 --> 00:01:34.849
He walked around the garden and returned to the house.

24
00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:38.132
Mad with love, he pounded on the door.

25
00:01:38.712 --> 00:01:40.994
He did not care if her father answered the door.

26
00:01:41.014 --> 00:01:43.456
"Cosette! Cosette!"

27
00:01:43.856 --> 00:01:45.458
cried Marius in a loud voice.

28
00:01:46.379 --> 00:01:47.580
There was no response.

29
00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:51.062
Nobody was in the garden, nobody in the house.

30
00:01:51.843 --> 00:01:55.566
Marius fixed his eyes on that house as dark and silent as a tomb.

31
00:01:56.567 --> 00:01:58.837
Feeling hopeless, he sat on the steps.

32
00:01:59.578 --> 00:02:04.582
"Since Cosette has gone," he said to himself, "there's nothing for me to do but die."

33
00:02:05.563 --> 00:02:08.985
Suddenly he heard a voice coming from the street beyond the garden gate.

34
00:02:09.006 --> 00:02:11.027
"Monsieur Marius!"

35
00:02:11.868 --> 00:02:12.428
He arose.

36
00:02:12.448 --> 00:02:21.036
"Yes?" "Monsieur Marius, your friends are expecting you at the barricade on the Rue de la Chanvrerie."

37
00:02:22.097 --> 00:02:23.618
The voice sounded like Eponine's.

38
00:02:24.198 --> 00:02:26.000
Marius rushed to the gate and looked out.

39
00:02:26.496 --> 00:02:30.357
He saw someone who looked like a young man rapidly disappearing down the street.

40
00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.498
What was this barricade?

41
00:02:33.178 --> 00:02:38.299
While Marius had been in despair, Courfeyrac and the others had joined what would later be called the

42
00:02:38.359 --> 00:02:40.660
Paris Uprising of 1832.

43
00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:47.082
A large group of students and workers decided to rebel against the monarchy, and they took their fight

44
00:02:47.242 --> 00:02:48.562
into the streets of Paris.

45
00:02:49.622 --> 00:02:56.956
Outside the Corinth Tavern, fifty men were building a barricade to block the Rue de la Chanvrerie.

46
00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:59.778
Iron bars were ripped from the grates in front of the tavern.

47
00:03:00.739 --> 00:03:02.780
Twenty yards of pavement were torn up.

48
00:03:03.561 --> 00:03:06.323
Piles of stones and barrels were also added.

49
00:03:07.583 --> 00:03:11.306
An omnibus was even tipped over and incorporated into the barricade.

50
00:03:12.347 --> 00:03:17.670
Despite all these preparations, the barricade did not exceed six or seven feet in height.

51
00:03:18.411 --> 00:03:20.953
Similar barricades were going up throughout Paris.

52
00:03:21.993 --> 00:03:28.153
When the barricade was completed, a table was dragged from the tavern, and Courfeyrac distributed ammunition.

53
00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:33.694
There was not much ammunition; each man received only thirty cartridges.

54
00:03:34.394 --> 00:03:36.075
A powder keg sat nearby.

55
00:03:37.235 --> 00:03:43.537
The fifty men in the Chanvrerie barricade loaded their guns and waited as darkness fell over Paris.

56
00:03:44.377 --> 00:03:45.317
Nothing happened.

57
00:03:45.898 --> 00:03:48.058
The government forces were taking their time.

58
00:03:49.038 --> 00:03:54.080
Among the men in the barricade was the street urchin Gavroche, who was also Eponine's brother.

59
00:03:55.008 --> 00:03:58.310
While the rebels waited for the attack, Gavroche looked around.

60
00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:02.812
Suddenly he recognized someone, a new recruit to the rebellion.

61
00:04:04.233 --> 00:04:07.875
Gavroche ran to Enjolras, one of the leaders in the barricade.

62
00:04:07.895 --> 00:04:10.016
"See that fellow over there?"

63
00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:12.317
Gavroche indicated a tall man.

64
00:04:12.337 --> 00:04:14.638
"I think he's a spy!

65
00:04:15.179 --> 00:04:19.141
He's really a policeman; two weeks ago he tried to arrest me."

66
00:04:20.141 --> 00:04:21.582
Enjolras approached the man.

67
00:04:21.602 --> 00:04:23.303
"What are you doing here?

68
00:04:23.943 --> 00:04:24.704
What's your name?"

69
00:04:25.408 --> 00:04:28.490
"I'm an officer of the government and my name is Javert."

70
00:04:29.611 --> 00:04:32.713
Enjolras gave a signal and four men pounced on Javert.

71
00:04:33.274 --> 00:04:35.255
They threw him to the ground and searched him.

72
00:04:36.216 --> 00:04:39.878
They found a piece of paper instructing him to look for the rebels' hideouts.

73
00:04:41.059 --> 00:04:46.923
"You are a spy, and you'll be shot ten minutes before the barricade is seized," said Enjolras.

74
00:04:47.984 --> 00:04:49.305
"Why don't you shoot me now?"

75
00:04:49.825 --> 00:04:50.606
asked Javert.

76
00:04:50.626 --> 00:04:53.788
"We don't want to waste the ammunition."

77
00:04:54.772 --> 00:04:57.714
By this time Marius was heading for the barricade.

78
00:04:58.314 --> 00:05:01.457
He knew it would be a dangerous place, but he no longer cared.

79
00:05:02.117 --> 00:05:04.719
It was clear that Cosette no longer loved him.

80
00:05:05.599 --> 00:05:08.021
She had left without sending him a single word.

81
00:05:08.561 --> 00:05:11.523
There was no excuse for this because she knew his address.

82
00:05:12.084 --> 00:05:14.805
He could not abandon his friends, who clearly needed him.

83
00:05:15.826 --> 00:05:21.190
They were perhaps a handful of men against an entire army that was defending the monarchy.

84
00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:24.612
Forty-three rebels crouched behind the barricade.

85
00:05:25.356 --> 00:05:29.018
The other seven were stationed in the two upper stories of the Corinth Tavern.

86
00:05:30.098 --> 00:05:33.259
Suddenly there was the sound of marching footsteps.

87
00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.421
A loud explosion burst over the barricade.

88
00:05:36.781 --> 00:05:37.801
The attack had begun!

89
00:05:38.842 --> 00:05:41.122
Two National Guards climbed over the barricade.

90
00:05:41.783 --> 00:05:43.483
One knocked Courfeyrac to the ground.

91
00:05:44.944 --> 00:05:47.085
The other threatened Gavroche with his bayonet.

92
00:05:47.865 --> 00:05:50.526
Two shots rang out, and the guards fell over.

93
00:05:51.187 --> 00:05:54.568
Marius had just entered the barricade and fired Javert's pistol.

94
00:05:55.816 --> 00:05:59.578
More soldiers entered the barricade, but Marius was out of ammunition.

95
00:06:00.199 --> 00:06:03.100
As he frantically looked around, a guard aimed at him.

96
00:06:04.081 --> 00:06:08.583
Suddenly a young workingman in velvet trousers reached out in front of Marius.

97
00:06:09.164 --> 00:06:12.645
When the gun fired, it was the workingman who fell to the ground.

98
00:06:13.606 --> 00:06:16.588
Marius looked around again and spotted the keg of gunpowder.

99
00:06:16.608 --> 00:06:19.429
"Clear out or I'll blow up the barricade!"

100
00:06:19.769 --> 00:06:20.310
he shouted.

101
00:06:21.370 --> 00:06:24.012
Everyone turned to look at him as he picked up a lit torch.

102
00:06:25.276 --> 00:06:29.239
"If you blow up the barricade, you'll blow up yourself too," said a soldier.

103
00:06:29.259 --> 00:06:30.820
"That's right."

104
00:06:31.301 --> 00:06:33.262
Marius waved the torch near the keg.

105
00:06:34.483 --> 00:06:39.847
The soldiers fled over the top of the barricade as fast as they could."Who's in charge here?"

106
00:06:40.267 --> 00:06:41.428
Marius asked the rebels.

107
00:06:42.509 --> 00:06:43.009
"You are!"

108
00:06:43.409 --> 00:06:45.571
said Enjolras, patting him on the back.

109
00:06:46.292 --> 00:06:47.252
Other men did too.

110
00:06:47.833 --> 00:06:49.074
Marius was a hero.

111
00:06:49.094 --> 00:06:50.955
"Monsieur Marius!"

112
00:06:51.395 --> 00:06:52.076
cried a voice.

113
00:06:52.776 --> 00:06:56.098
Marius recognized Eponine's voice, but he didn't see her anywhere.

114
00:06:56.118 --> 00:06:59.341
"At your feet," said Eponine.

115
00:07:00.041 --> 00:07:01.102
Marius bent over.

116
00:07:01.622 --> 00:07:05.284
The torchlight revealed the face of the young man in the velvet trousers.

117
00:07:05.304 --> 00:07:08.487
"Eponine! What are you doing here?"

118
00:07:08.507 --> 00:07:10.028
"I'm dying."

119
00:07:10.048 --> 00:07:12.069
"I'll carry you into the tavern."

120
00:07:12.089 --> 00:07:14.811
"No She struggled to talk.

121
00:07:14.831 --> 00:07:16.312
"It's too late.

122
00:07:17.192 --> 00:07:22.436
I used my hand to stop the bullet intended for you."

123
00:07:23.892 --> 00:07:27.234
"No one dies from a wounded hand," protested Marius.

124
00:07:27.254 --> 00:07:32.578
"The bullet entered my chest," she said weakly.

125
00:07:32.598 --> 00:07:39.062
"I didn't want you to go to that garden, and yet I showed you where she lived.

126
00:07:39.903 --> 00:07:42.185
But it's all right now.

127
00:07:43.325 --> 00:07:48.649
Nobody will get out alive from this barricade—not even my brother.

128
00:07:49.670 --> 00:07:55.974
I sent you here so we could die together because I've always been in love with you."

129
00:07:57.134 --> 00:07:59.215
Marius gazed at her with compassion.

130
00:07:59.235 --> 00:08:03.137
"I have a letter for you."

131
00:08:03.998 --> 00:08:05.359
Eponine held out her hand.

132
00:08:05.379 --> 00:08:11.942
"I was supposed to deliver it yesterday, but I didn't want it to reach you.

133
00:08:12.623 --> 00:08:20.067
Now that I know we'll be reunited after death, I don't want you to be angry with me."

134
00:08:21.247 --> 00:08:25.246
Eponine died, and Marius took the letter from her hand.
